;
; Counts full low-to-high pulse transitions on one input pin via the state
; machine's X scratch register, used as a free-running down-counter --
; the PIO instruction set has no direct increment, only `JMP X--`
; (unconditionally decrements X, branches only if the pre-decrement value
; was non-zero). Firmware (drivers/rp2350_pio_edge_counter.c) initializes
; X to 0xFFFFFFFF on start and reads the running total as
; `0xFFFFFFFF - X`, snapshotting X on demand via pio_sm_exec()-injected
; instructions rather than a continuous FIFO/DMA stream, since a channel
; read() is a low-rate periodic poll, not a high-rate capture.
;
; `jmp x-- top` as the loop's last instruction, immediately followed by
; `.wrap`, is deliberate: when X is non-zero the jump is taken straight
; back to `top`; when X was zero (wrapping to 0xFFFFFFFF) the jump is not
; taken, but falling through past the last instruction before `.wrap`
; triggers the same wrap-to-`top` -- both paths land back at the loop
; start either way, so the loop is unconditional regardless of which path
; is taken.
;
; Correctness caveat: this program has not been run against real RP2350
; PIO hardware or a simulator -- see drivers/include/drivers/uic_driver.h
; and docs/releases/v0.5.1.md T6 for the project's standing pre-hardware
; disclosure convention.
.program uic_pulse_counter
.wrap_target
top:
    wait 0 pin, 0
    wait 1 pin, 0
    jmp x-- top
.wrap
